Ladybird now takes the content size suggestion of a replaced flex item
with a percentage width or max-width from its uncompressed size. Blink
takes the content size suggestion from
MinMaxSizesFunc(SizeType::kContent), the item’s min-content size rather
than its contribution, so a percentage max-width doesn’t compress it;
Gecko’s nsFlexContainerFrame::PartiallyResolveAutoMinSize() computes it
with ComputeSize() at an auto inline size, where a percentage max-width
resolves against the container rather than against zero.

Run in Chrome 157.0.8103.79, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5
(Playwright’s build), all three agree with Ladybird now on the test’s
cases, except for an image with width: 100% next to a 300px sibling,
where Firefox shrinks it to 100x50 and Chrome and WebKit keep it at
200x100, as Ladybird does.
